thank you for talking to me about the  show i love the show on  two levels the whole nostalgia factor  from reading the books when i was  younger and how it also proves the good  stories and good character as a  universal universal no matter what your  agents  so what has it meant to you guys to get  to be a part of the babysitter's club  what's the coolest thing about being a  part of this world and doing this show  yeah i mean like you mentioned i think  it brings so much like nostalgia to  like all the um  individuals who have read the books  before and it also kind of introduces  introduces the books to like  uh and the stories of the babysitters to  a new generation as well and i also  think it's so great how like inclusive  and like diverse  um  this just the babysitter's club is in  general and how we get to see the  stories of  all these girls and how they handle each  of their problems because i think it's  so real and um  others watching can all relate to it  mo hit so many good points but i'll just  add that  these stories are really classic and  incredible and these characters are so  lovable and it's amazing just to be able  to bring them to life again for a new  generation also like you had said it's  just it's such an honor i feel very  lucky  you were pretty much able to make this  first season in your own little bubble  while the fans of the books didn't  really know what to expect but now with  the second season there's a certain  level of expectation  so did you guys feel an added sense of  pressure and responsibility to live up  to that or were you just excited about  getting to dive in even deeper  um i've been just excited and also like  um in season one we couldn't talk about  it at all because  the complete surprise we only announced  it once we'd already finished filming so  this time around it was really nice to  be able to  post when we were hanging out out of  filming um and just be able to say that  we were all together because um it's  