hrough  any nerves that we had and and i can say  that that's lasted through  until even just today like  being nervous about an interview we all  help each other through through all of  those things because we're going through  it at the exact same time so i think  being together and being with people  that we love definitely helped with that  but um  yeah just as soon as we started filming  it felt like home to me and being  being stacey felt like home so it was  incredible just to be able to finally  bring it to life rather than just being  in an audition room  what do you guys most love about your  character and what quality of theirs do  you wish you had for yourself  um well i really admire stacy's  confidence and i think she's also a very  responsible hard-working girl so i think  those are incredible traits that she  holds amongst many others but um i  strive to be as confident as she is  yeah i think for claudia she's just so  like unapologetically her own self and  she really doesn't care about what  others have to say about her as much  and that's something that i admire and i  try to you know incorporate i guess into  my own  like when it comes to my own  self-confidence as well  momona claudia becomes closer with her  sister this season and we get to learn a  little bit more about their relationship  together  what did you enjoy about that dynamic  and getting to see how different the two  of them are but how they still can  really love each other  yeah i mean i think the first season  dived into that a little bit but this  season we were really able to see  um an even stronger connection between  the two sisters and um i think  uh sorry i lost my my channel hold on  yeah i think even though they're just  they're so different they learn to  really love each other for their own  qualities and you know i think claudia  really admires janine in ways that maybe  she can exactly like say right to her  but i think there's this one really  beautiful moment when she tells janine  that it's like no matter what like she's  there for her and i think that was  really great  she i also really love that we get to  see the role that diabetes plays in  stacy's life it's something she just has  to learn to live with and figure out how  to balance so what does it mean to you  to be telling this story and what do you  hope other young people get from  watching how she handles it  it is such an honor to be able to  portray stacy who is such an iconic  character and such a  incredible representation of people who  have type 1 diabetes and and young girls  who are dealing with that so  um aside from that i think it's just a  very real thing to be coming to terms  with something about yourself that you  can't change and you can't control and  you have to just learn to love and i  think stacy does a really good job of  doing exactly that and i hope people can  see her on screen just  fully taking charge and and not  apologizing for who she is and they can  learn to do that in their own lives as  well  do you guys have your own personal wish  list for your character and things you  still want to learn about them or get to  do or explore with them in the future  no  yeah that's a good question i think  uh  just  continuing and like watching how they  they transition into  their later teen years if if we do get  the opportunity to do more um i think  that would be interesting because you  know as they grow up and grow older  there's going to be new  uh challenges that each of the  characters face and i will  would love to see kind of  uh how the  events of this season could affect um  claudia in the later seasons if if we  get a chance to do more  um yeah i think just seeing the  friendships continue to evolve because i  know they have from the beginning of  season one to the end of season two  they've grown so much in real life and  on screen so i think it it's just always  incredible to see those evolve and to  see our our group of girls 